"font-weight:600\">Willie Pennington</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Chief Communications Officer</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Facilitator</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Herminio Strand</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Senior Manager of Marketing Programs</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Contractor</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Nora Nielsen</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Chief People Officer</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Leadership Development Consultant (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Ayo Shelton</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Associate, Communications</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Retirement Plan Advisor (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Agenda</h5><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 1</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">CEO Succession Plan Review — Emergency &amp; Long-Term</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The committee discussed the findings of the recent audit related to the CEO Succession Plan Review — Emergency &amp; Long-Term. Tuyen Marks summarized the 158 findings and management&#x27;s proposed remediation plan. The committee endorsed the plan and requested quarterly progress updates.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To approve for transformation:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Foundation Audit Committee authorizes a share repurchase program of up to $158M of the company&#x27;s common stock.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Willie Pennington &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Tuyen Marks</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 7 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 1 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 2</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Share Repurchase Program Authorization</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Share Repurchase Program Authorization was a review of the company&#x27;s compliance with the Bipartisan Campaign Reform Act. The committee reviewed the company&#x27;s electioneering communications and confirmed that they were in compliance.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To approve for KPIs:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Foundation Audit Committee has reviewed and discussed the quarterly financial statements with management and the independent auditors.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Benjamin Hall &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Ayo Shelton</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 5 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 3 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 3</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Government Affairs Update — 13 Legislation</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Government Affairs Update — 13 Legislation was a review of the company&#x27;s performance against its ESG goals. Nora Nielsen reported that the company had met 158 of its 20 targets for the year. The committee discussed strategies for addressing the shortfalls.</p></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Action Items</h5><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th style=\"width:2rem\">#</th><th>Description</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">1</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Prepare a communication for employees regarding the upcoming open enrollment period</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Efrat Song</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">2008-03-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">2</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Prepare a report on the diversity of the leadership pipeline</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Filip Grant</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">2008-02-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">3</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Analyze the effectiveness of the company&#x27;s internal mobility program</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Carol Cooper</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">2008-03-28</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem 1.2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem\"><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:#333;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.5rem\">There being no further business, a motion to adjourn was made and carried unanimously. Meeting adjourned at 12:30 PM CT.</p><p style=\"font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;color:#555\"><strong>Next meeting:</strong> 2008-02-19</p><div><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#888;margin-bottom:.25rem\">Respectfully submitted,</p><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.1rem\">Ayo Shelton</p><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#666;margin-bottom:.75rem\">Associate, Communications, Retirement Plan Advisor (External)</p><div style=\"display:flex;gap:2rem\"><div><div style=\"width:160px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Signature</div></div><div><div style=\"width:120px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Approved: ___________</div></div></div></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><a href=\"/archive/2008/01/20/data-privacy-and-compliance-impact-assessment-2478/